<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramiro I of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 790–850</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramiro I was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 842 to 850. He seized the throne after the death of Alfonso II, defeating a rival claimant, and faced revolts by nobles, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> raid on the Galician coast in 844, which he repelled, and warfare with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a>. His reign is best remembered for the pre-Romanesque buildings on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monte-naranco">Monte Naranco</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oviedo">Oviedo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramiro-i-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Ramiro I of Asturias" width="301" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sinatura_de_Ramiro_I_de_Oviedo_no_Celeiro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
